---
import SealedSection from '../seal/SealedSection.astro';
import SectionHead from '../ui/SectionHead.astro';
import SubHead from '../ui/SubHead.astro';
import Shot from '../ui/Shot.astro';
import settingsShot from '../../assets/shots/settings.svg';
import exitCardShot from '../../assets/shots/exit-card.svg';
import footerShot from '../../assets/shots/footer.svg';
import roleManagerShot from '../../assets/shots/role-manager.svg';

const sealText =
  'Quality of life: smaller features you would otherwise add through a skills.md. First-run trust gate, prompt library, one composer history for prompts and commands, repo map, work-discipline prompt section, identity block, capability auth probes, diff in the approval prompt, a todo panel that only trusts assistant text, sessions, Markdown session export, opt-in per-goal auto-commit, an opt-in post-end test pass with a fast-model report and a bounded fix loop, /settings with provenance, no alt bindings ever, /help guarded by a test, caveman mode, per-project session toggles, classifier verdicts in the internal-work feed, a shell panel for !cmd with the raw output, transcript rows stamped when they happen with durations, token budgets per model in the footer, oversized tool output kept out of the context with ReadResult to read the rest, WebFetch that answers a question instead of returning the page, desktop notifications, voice input to the composer, /skills, /plugin, /mcp and /sandbox, and a self-update that stays in its asset family.';

const groups = [
  {
    title: 'Trust and safety',
    items: [
      ['first-run trust gate', 'A directory Belai has never seen blocks startup until you say yes, before any settings merge, repo scan or auto-started process.'],
      ['todo panel that only trusts assistant text', "The todo list only changes based on the assistant's own text. Tool output cannot update it."],
      ['classifier verdicts in the feed', 'When a result is blocked, the internal-work feed shows which phase blocked it and what it returned.'],
      ['one line per decision', 'Each row has an icon for the activity, coloured by the kind of work, the outcome with a mark that reads without colour, and who decided: the Jev model by name, a chat model by name, or belai for plain code. The summary shortens first on a narrow terminal, and ctrl+o adds a dim line with the full model, score and cause.'],
      ['!cmd gets its own shell panel', 'A !cmd shows its raw output in a panel, live while it runs. The model only gets the sanitised, classified copy, and the panel marks the output "not sent" when that copy is withheld. ctrl+o expands it, ctrl+c copies it and ctrl+s saves it.'],
      ['desktop notifications', 'Opt in with notifications.enabled and Belai tells you when a permission ask, a question or a plan is waiting, or when a goal ends. Every notification is written from a fixed template.'],
      ['self-update stays in its family', 'A guardrails binary updates to the next guardrails build, so it keeps its embedded model.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Prompts and the composer',
    items: [
      ['prompt library as files', 'Prompts are files in the repository, so they are versioned and reviewed like code.'],
      ['one history for everything you typed', 'Up recalls prompts, !shell commands, !!processes and /slash commands in the order you ran them, across restarts, with repeats kept once at their newest position.'],
      ['work-discipline prompt section', 'The system prompt tells the model to read the exact lines it will change, batch its reads, make the edits it is sure of first, and report what changed.'],
      ['identity block', 'Every system prompt names the harness, provider and model in use.'],
      ['images in the composer', 'Type @ and pick a PNG or JPEG, press ctrl+v to attach the image on the clipboard, or drop a file on the terminal. Belai checks the image, scales it and re-encodes it, and never sends it to the classifier. The chip shows the size, tokens and whether the model gets it, at most eight go with a prompt, and the session file keeps a marker and no pixels.'],
      ['no alt bindings', 'No shortcut uses the alt key, so terminals that capture alt do not swallow keystrokes.'],
      ['voice input', 'Hold F11 and speak. A speech model written in pure Go is built into the release binary (every family but the plain belai build) and your words appear in the composer as you say them, then a fast model tidies them and its reply streams over the raw text. A microphone pulses and the frame ripples when it hears you, dictated prompts are lilac with the raw transcript one ctrl+o away, and typing anything cancels it all at once. Turn on the wake word to have it act only on "Hey, Belay", say stop, option 2, submit, skip, approve or deny to answer an ask, or name a skill, crew or mode and Jev runs it when the match is very close. /voice debug shows the level meter and the key events when nothing comes out. Audio stays in memory on your machine.'],
      ['read aloud', 'Run /tts on, then press ctrl+b to hear any reply, or let belai read each final report when a turn ends. A player card in the thread shows the position: click the bar to scrub, pick 0.75x to 2x, and say stop to silence it. Audio is cached on your machine, so a replay is instant and works offline. Reading uses the Microsoft read-aloud service, so the text you have read is sent there, and you agree to that once with /tts on.'],
      ['caveman mode', 'An optional voice that makes replies short and plain.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Context and cost',
    items: [
      ['harness-computed repo map', 'Paths, counts, detected commands, the test suites with their framework and test-file convention, and git metadata, with no file contents.'],
      ['oversized output kept out of context', 'A long build log, page or PR thread goes into the conversation as its first and last lines plus a reference. ReadResult reads the rest by line range or pattern when it is needed. Bash keeps the end of its output too, so a failing test summary is never the part that gets cut.'],
      ['WebFetch answers the question', 'Give WebFetch a prompt and a small model with no tools reads the page and returns the answer. The page itself never enters the conversation, and the answer is classified like the page would be.'],
      ['token budgets per model', 'Session, day and month allowances per provider and model, counted across every model call and every belai process, shown right-aligned in the footer: teal on pace, amber when spend runs ahead of the clock, red when spent.'],
      ['session intelligence', 'Plan limits with their reset times, pace, trend, runway and today, week and 30 day totals. The footer cycle ends on it under any routing, with or without a budget, and f12 opens a pane with bars and sparklines.'],
      ['capability auth probes', 'A small test request checks that a model supports a capability before Belai relies on it.'],
    ],
  },
  {
    title: 'Sessions and settings',
    items: [
      ['/settings with provenance', 'Settings sit in groups on a rail, or on a tab strip in a narrow terminal, and each group fits one screen at any height. A value that differs from its default shows the layer it came from, and the detail pane says where a change is saved. Press / to filter and m to list only the values you changed.'],
      ['session toggles per project', 'Toggles such as guardrails and ask-permission are saved for each repository.'],
      ['session export', 'Type /export to write the current session (or another by id) as deterministic Markdown under .vulnetix/exports; belai -export <id> prints it to stdout.'],
      ['opt-in per-goal auto-commit', 'Turn on auto-commit per task in /settings and every completed goal is committed as one conventional commit of exactly the files it changed. The setting is global, so a repository cannot turn it on.'],
      ['post-end test pass', 'Turn on tests.post_end and a completed goal, plan or session runs the tests Belai detected in the repository. A pass gets a short report from the fast model, and a failure starts a bounded fix loop on the main model with the classified output attached. The pass is off until you turn it on, the exit code decides pass or fail, and a repository can only switch it off.'],
      ['search reference documents by meaning', 'List documents in an agent profile, and Belai also indexes the scanner output in the project\'s .vulnetix directory and the files you attach with @. Grep, Glob and Read then return the passages that resemble what the agent asked for, beside their usual answer, in every mode and in fleet workers. It is pure Go with nothing to download. Each passage is checked by the security classifier once, when it is indexed, and a search calls no model. Three sizes in /settings set how much a host keeps and returns.'],
      ['label and browse what is indexed', 'Belai tags each indexed document with its type, language and size, and with the topics it is about, from a vocabulary of about three hundred. A pattern matcher written in Go does this with no model. With a Jev decision backend configured it also shows the backend a sample of the document and picks the topics in one request, and it asks only about documents the security classifier already admitted. /knowledge lists the documents of this project, of every project on the host or of your agents, filters by label such as topic:jwt or type:test, and searches with the same Grep, Glob and Read code a model uses, so you see what it would see. The screen only reads the indexes.'],
      ['timestamps and durations in the transcript', 'Each transcript row is stamped when its event happened, and tool calls, model replies and classifier decisions record how long they took, so a slow session shows where the time went.'],
      ['diff in the approval prompt', 'The approval prompt shows the diff of the change as well as the path.'],
      ['/help guarded by a test', 'A test compares the help text with the real key bindings.'],
      ['/skills, /plugin, /mcp and /sandbox', 'One command each shows the installed skills, the plugins and their state, the MCP servers and their tools, and the sandbox policy commands run under.'],
    ],
  },
];

const total = groups.reduce((n, g) => n + g.items.length, 0);
---

<SealedSection label="qol" sealText={sealText} id="qol">
  <SectionHead title="Quality of life">
    Smaller features you would otherwise add yourself through a <code class="mono">skills.md</code>. Each
    one is implemented and tested in this repository.
  </SectionHead>

  <div class="mt-head">
    {groups.map((g) => (
      <details class="deep deep--wide">
        <summary>
          <span class="min-w-0">
            <span class="block font-semibold">{g.title} <span class="mono ml-2 text-xs font-normal text-vx-ink/70">{g.items.length} of {total}</span></span>
            <span class="mt-1 line-clamp-2 block font-sans text-sm font-normal text-vx-ink/70">{g.items.map(([title]) => title).join(', ')}</span>
          </span>
        </summary>
        <div class="deep__body">
          <dl class="m-0 grid gap-x-10 @4xl:grid-cols-2">
            {g.items.map(([title, detail]) => (
              <div class="border-b border-vx-ink/15 py-4">
                <dt class="mono text-sm font-semibold">{title}</dt>
                <dd class="m-0 mt-1 text-sm text-vx-ink/80">{detail}</dd>
              </div>
            ))}
          </dl>
        </div>
      </details>
    ))}
  </div>

  <SubHead title="Long sessions">
    <code class="mono">/compact</code> writes a summary that must include a goal, next steps and critical
    context, and a summary missing any of them is rejected. Sessions are named after the work done in them.
  </SubHead>
  <div class="mt-head grid gap-8 @4xl:grid-cols-2 @4xl:items-start">
    <div class="min-w-0">
      <p class="text-vx-ink/80">
        A message sent mid-turn is queued onto the running turn, and the exit card shows the command to
        resume the session. Long sessions stay affordable in four ways.
      </p>
      <ul class="mt-4 list-none border-t border-vx-ink/60 p-0 text-vx-ink/85">
        <li class="border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-3">Oversized tool output is replaced once, when it arrives, so the cached prefix of every later request is unchanged.</li>
        <li class="border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-3">Old tool results are cleared in large steps.</li>
        <li class="border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-3">The conversation is compacted at 70% of the window, first by pruning the tool calls and results the work ahead no longer needs when a decision backend is configured, and by a summary otherwise.</li>
        <li class="border-b border-vx-ink/20 py-3">When a provider still reports an overflow, Belai compacts and retries instead of ending the turn.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-6 text-vx-ink/80">
        <code class="mono">/tree</code> shows a session as branches. Pick an earlier reply and the conversation
        carries on from there; pick a prompt and it returns to the composer to be reworded. The session file
        only grows, so everything written before stays in it, and <code class="mono">f</code> copies a branch
        into a new session. Files on disk keep their current contents. Editors connected over ACP can type
        <code class="mono">/tree</code> too.
      </p>
    </div>
    <Shot src={exitCardShot.src} alt="The branded session-end card" caption="exit card, resume command" />
  </div>
  <details class="deep deep--wide">
    <summary>Three more screens: settings, the internal-work feed and the footer</summary>
    <div class="deep__body">
  <div class="mt-4 grid max-w-[1000px] gap-6">
    <Shot src={settingsShot.src} alt="The settings screen showing provenance per value" caption="/settings, provenance per value" />
    <Shot src={roleManagerShot.src} alt="The internal-work feed: one line per decision with an activity icon, an outcome mark and the model that decided" caption="internal-work feed, Jev decisions named by model" />
    <Shot src={footerShot.src} alt="The status footer with chips and an amber day budget" caption="status footer, guardrails on, day budget amber" />
  </div>
    </div>
  </details>
</SealedSection>
